    "body": "Problem:\r\nWhen `unpacker_parse_redraw()` fails, it closes the unpacker without setting `unpack_error`, so `chan_close_on_err()` gets a NULL message. A pending request fails with an empty error (`RPC: (null)`).\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42173 fixed the crash that followed (advancing the closed unpacker), but not the silent close itself.\r\n\r\nRepro:\r\nSelf-attach (`nvim_ui_attach` on a loopback `sockconnect()` channel) closes the channel without a visible reason, either while `nvim_ui_attach` is pending or at the next redraw.\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\nSet an error msg when `unpacker_parse_redraw()` fails.\r\n\r\nNote:\r\nSelf-attach fails for accidental reasons, not by design:\r\n- An incoming \"redraw\" notif is always parsed \"as a UI client\" (`handle_ui_client_redraw`), whose `grid_line` buffer is only allocated in a UI client process. A loopback channel is both ends, so it parses its own redraw stream as if it were the TUI.\r\n- Even if parsing worked, `parse_msgpack()` drops redraw events unless `ui_client_attached`, and a `sockconnect()` client has no notification callback.\r\n\r\nfix https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/31726",
